# JEE sim → user version (four layers, one sim per agent)

Full procedure, verify gates and output contract: **`.cursor/commands/jee-sim-user-version.md`** — read it before editing. This rule is the short form for when the command isn't invoked explicitly.

## What you are building

One sim → `sim-use-builds/<same-basename>.html`, carrying four layers applied in this order:

1. **Guided-inquiry button contract** — `#shell-lecture` and all lecture machinery replaced by the `#btn-gi` / `#btn-cg` pair (mutually exclusive, GI boots active); hooks `__giOff` / `__freeExplore` / `__giResume` / `__cgReveals` published from the sim's scope; Finish routes through `__giOff`. Card content is **copy-polish only** (trim >90-word cards, >60-word feedback — never restructure; an explicit SME-grammar content pass instead follows `Sim_use_version_skills/guided-inquiry/SKILL.md` + `references/golden-flows.md`).
2. **Controls tutorial** — purple callout walking every control/readout one at a time, hidden-until-its-turn, `__fullReset` wired additively to Reset.
3. **Welcome overlay** — three glass mode cards over a per-sim hero canvas drawn from the sim's own equations, plus the read-aloud player.
4. **Card voiceover + Auto** — Listen row above `.inq-nav`, two-row controls-guide nav, shared speech engine; Auto walks each flow hands-free and **never answers a prediction** for the student.

## Specification (single source of truth — copy the blocks, don't re-derive)

- `Sim_use_version_skills/guided-inquiry/SKILL.md` + `references/implementation.md`
- `Sim_use_version_skills/controls-tutorial/SKILL.md` + `references/implementation.md` (§1–§4 base layers, **§6** voiceover, §6.4 identifier map, §6.4b watcher shells, §6.5 Chrome TTS pitfalls)
- `Sim_use_version_skills/welcome-overlay/SKILL.md` + `references/implementation.md`

Validated exemplars: **C-series** → `sim-use-builds/C203-refraction-and-snells-law.html`; **L-series** → `sim-use-builds/L30-the-coriolis-force.html`.

## Non-negotiable

- Never modify the original sim — `cp` first, edit only the copy. Other agents work sibling files in parallel; no repo-wide replacements.
- Small targeted edits only. A whole-file write of a ~300 KB sim fails mid-response and corrupts the output.
- No git operations.
- Never introduce third-party sim-source names (PhET, Collision Lab, Gases Intro, Pickup Coil, Colorado…) — these files were scrubbed for copyright. Re-grep before reporting.
- Physics kernel, `window.__audit`, `engine-manifest` / `engine-inline` / `shell-runtime` blocks stay byte-identical apart from the sanctioned deltas.

## Gates — all must pass before reporting

```bash
cd Sim_use_version_skills                       # jsdom lives here
node guided-inquiry/scripts/verify.js    '../sim-use-builds/<b>.html' --baseline '../<original>'
node controls-tutorial/scripts/verify.js '../sim-use-builds/<b>.html' --baseline '../<original>'
node welcome-overlay/scripts/verify.js   '../sim-use-builds/<b>.html'
```

Then the **mandatory real-Chrome flow probe** (jsdom cannot see a boot-time exception that kills both flows):

```bash
python3 -m http.server 8734 ; node tools/flow-probe.mjs 9500 <basename>.html
```

Plus `node --check` on every inline script, unique ids (`btn-gi`, `btn-cg`, `inq-voice`, `inq-auto`, `cg-auto`, `cg-rew`, `cg-fwd`, `cg-voice-play`, `welcome-overlay` — exactly once each), all hooks present, copyright grep clean, original unchanged. Never ship with a lowered bar; if a gate can't pass, stop and say why.
